<title>USA: W.R. Grace completes sale of polymers unit.</title>
<headline>W.R. Grace completes sale of polymers unit.</headline>
<dateline>BOCA RATON, Fla. 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>W.R. Grace &amp; Co said on Friday it completed the sale of its specialty polymers business to National Starch and Chemical Co, a subsidiary of Unilever Group, for $148 million in cash.</p>
<p>The unit, Grace Specialty Polymers, had 1996 sales of $73 million.</p>
<p>National Starch, based in Bridgewater, N.J., makes adhesives, resins, specialty chemicals, electronic materials and specialty and industrial and food starches.</p>
</text>
